  "description": "UQEDON crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C118 H136 Cl2 Co6 Er4 N14 O36,C2 H3 N1,6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Co1 (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Er1 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 3 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.153-3.850 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.65-114.66°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Co6Er4(HL)4(pdmH)2(pdm)8Cl2]·CH3CN·6H2O (C118H148Cl2Co6Er4N14O42; Mr = 3528.05; CCDC formula C118H136Cl2Co6Er4N14O36·C2H3N·6(H2O)). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
